} Hỗ trợ triển khai và giám sát các biện pháp kiểm soát an toàn thông tin và yêu cầu tuân thủ. Hỗ trợ thực hiện đánh giá rủi ro CNTT và cập nhật Ma trận Rủi ro & Kiểm soát CNTT (IT Risk & Control Matrix). Hỗ trợ theo dõi lỗ hổng bảo mật, xử lý sự cố an toàn thông tin và giám sát việc khắc phục. Tham gia xây dựng, cập nhật các chính sách, quy trình và tiêu chuẩn an toàn thông tin. Chuẩn bị báo cáo, hồ sơ kiểm toán và các tài liệu liên quan đến an toàn thông tin. Hỗ trợ tổ chức đào tạo nâng cao nhận thức về an toàn thông tin và thực hiện các công việc khác theo phân công của Quản lý. Tốt nghiệp Đại học chuyên ngành Công nghệ Thông tin, An toàn Thông tin hoặc các ngành liên quan. Có từ 0-1 năm kinh nghiệm trong lĩnh vực An toàn thông tin, An ninh mạng hoặc các vị trí CNTT liên quan. Có kiến thức cơ bản về bảo mật mạng, bảo mật hệ thống, bảo mật ứng dụng và các mối đe dọa an ninh mạng. Có hiểu biết về các tiêu chuẩn bảo mật như ISO 27001, PCI-DSS, OWASP hoặc ITIL là một lợi thế. Có kỹ năng phân tích, giải quyết vấn đề và giao tiếp tốt. Có khả năng đọc hiểu tài liệu chuyên ngành bằng tiếng Anh Ngành nghề: CNTT - Phần mềm Kinh nghiệm: 1 Năm Cấp bậc: Nhân viên Hình thức: Nhân viên chính thức Địa điểm: Hà Nội

Top 3 Reasons To Join Us
Gain very attractive salary and benefits;
Be a developer, not a coder;
Excellent environment and team to help you grow.
The Job Projects you could work on Coding infrastructure automation with CDK, and Bitbucket Pipelines CI/CD; Improving our Elastic Monitoring or building new metrics; Helping release managers deploy and fix new versions of the various Repeat apps/microservices; Plan, prepare for, and execute the migration from Amazon EC2 virtual machines running on AWS to cloud-native container-based deployments with Amazon ECS; Develop a relationship with a product group, define their SLAs, share data on those SLAs and improve their reliability Responsibilities Run our infrastructure with AWS CDK, Bitbucket Pipelines CI/CD, and Kubernetes; Build monitoring that alerts on symptoms rather than on outages; Document every action so your findings turn into repeatable actions and then into automation; Improve operational processes (such as deployments and upgrades) to make them as boring as possible; Design, build and maintain core infrastructure that enables scaling to support hundreds of thousands of concurrent users; Debug production issues across services and levels of the stack; Plan the growth of the product’s infrastructure. Your Skills and Experience Think about systems: edge cases, failure modes, behaviors, specific implementations; Know your way around Linux and the Unix Shell; Know what configuration management systems like Chef and Ansible are used for; Strong programming skills in Shell, Typescript, and Python; Have good English communication skills; Have an urge to collaborate and communicate asynchronously; Have an urge to document all the things so you don’t need to learn the same thing twice; Have an enthusiastic, go-for-it attitude. When you see something broken, you can’t help but fix it; Have an urge to deliver quickly and effectively, and iterate fast; Share our values, and work in accordance with those values; Have experience with Apache/Nginx, HAProxy, Docker, Kubernetes, CDK, or similar technologies; Ability to use Bitbucket. Why You'll Love Working Here Remote work model; Full social insurance including probationary period; 12 days of annual leave and 3 additional special holidays (Swedish National Day, Christmas Eve & your Birthday); Annual leave increases with loyalty; Premium health care package for employees & family members; English, professional working environment.

Top 3 Reasons To Join Us
Gain very attractive salary and benefits;
Be a developer, not a coder;
Excellent environment and team to help you grow.
The Job Project Description : A web service for talent solutions, and you will work for the Data Management team responsible for handling various data-related tasks. The team maintains and governs data, providing solutions for processing, integration, and data services. They collaborate with the infrastructure/platform team to deploy AWS services and manage relationships with vendors to maintain managed services. Responsible for deploying and maintaining the data platform, in terms of auth of DBMS, data processing or access tools, applications and frameworks, such as batch and stream jobs on an ETL framework, metadata management tools, BI tools, AWS resources for hosting those tools, etc. Collaborate closely with data platform software engineers and our infrastructure/platform squad that maintains the entire infrastructure. Your Skills and Experience More than 5 years of working experience as a SRE/ DevOps Engineer, and it would be a plus if you have experience with data platform; Familiar with AWS, especially IAM, ECS, EKS, Lambda, RDS, CloudWatch (rich experience on AWS is a must; GCP or Azure experience is a plus); Rich experience in deploying containerized applications/services and very familiar with operations on Kubernetes; Rich experience in infra-as-code, familiar with IT automation systems like Scalr, Terraform or its alternatives, proficient in configuring and maintaining CI/CD flows (experience with ArgoCD is a plus); Good understanding of cloud architecture and infrastructure, and can design and maintain/handle the SLA/SLO, HA/DR of services; Good knowledge of cloud security, familiarity with SSO (experience with Auth0, Azure AD, Okta, etc.), authentication/ authorization mechanisms like SAML/OIDC, and OAuth; Experience in deploying, integrating and maintaining data processing and ML frameworks like Airflow, Puppet, Metabase, Databricks, Snowflake, Metaflow, MLflow, etc is a plus. Why You'll Love Working Here Remote work model and flexible working hours; Full social insurance, including probationary period; 12 days of annual leave and 3 additional special holidays (Swedish National Day, Christmas Eve & your Birthday); Annual leave increases with loyalty; Premium health care package for employees & family members; English, professional working environment; Opportunities to gain hands-on experience in cutting-edge technologies.
